  "facts": [
    "Opened March 2005, the Heathrow Airside Road Tunnel spans 1.42 kilometres, linking the airside roads of Terminals 1, 2 and 3 to those of Terminal 5, a critical artery for security‑cleared vehicles.",
    "Engineered between 1999 and 2004 by BAA, Amec, Laing O'Rourke, Morgan Est‑Vinci and Mott MacDonald, the tunnel features twin 60‑metre cut‑and‑cover boxes at each end and 1.3‑kilometre bored sections.",
    "A 9.16‑metre Herrenknecht earth‑pressure‑balance machine bored the 8.1‑metre diameter tunnels, whose 0.45‑metre thick bolted concrete lining had to withstand proximity to the surface and a 3‑metre overpass above the Heathrow Express tunnel."
  ],
